note "After James Urquhart, Flow Architectures, figure 3-24, p. 71" [0.03, 0.04]
%% Redrawn from "Our final map of the current state of flow needs" (O'Reilly, 2021), checked link for
%% link against the figure at high resolution on 17 Oct. Producer and consumer both need the flow
%% integration; the producer also reaches the sink and the consumer the source. The integration
%% rests on the interface and the protocol; the interface on discovery and the logical connection;
%% the protocol on the two formats. Source, sink and the logical connection run through the
%% processor; the processor feeds the queue; and six lines fan into infrastructure. Two of those six
%% (from the logical connection and from the source) are read off a dense drawing and stay a judgement.
